((date 2026-09-03) (slug exit-basis-d1d2-correctness)
 (hypothesis
  "Not a performance hypothesis. Records the USER-DIRECTED (2026-09-03, session start: 'yes - work autonomously' on the P0 of dev/notes/next-session-priorities-2026-09-03.md) correctness flip of two exit-basis defaults: sim_exit_fill_next_open false -> true (D1: a Market exit decided on a Friday tick was filling on the Saturday calendar step against the RETAINED Friday bar at Friday's OPEN, a price that predates the decision, and the trade was stamped Saturday) and stops_config.stop_skip_entry_bar false -> true (D2: fills run before the strategy each step, so a ticket filled intraday at E was already Holding when the stop runner read the same day's completed bar, and the entry bar's pre-fill low 'stopped out' the position on its own entry bar). Both defects were measured on the 26y arc rerun (dev/experiments/arc-rerun-2026-09-01/README.md sections D1 and D2, landed in PR #2645) and fixed behind default-off flags in PRs #2644 (D1) and #2642 (D2). This entry exists because the flips bypass the normal R3 gate (experiment-flag-discipline.md) as correctness fixes, and the ledger is what the next experiment session reads: every arm written after 2026-09-03 that does not pin these two knobs runs on the next-open exit fill + entry-bar-skip basis, NOT the stale-Friday-open basis every earlier recorded run used.")
 (base_scenario
  "arc-rerun-2026-09-01 26y top-3000 PIT-2000 arc bundle (results/arc26y-s0) + the 2026-08-24 record baseline, Saturday-dated exits repriced at the next trading open with quantities held fixed (results/reprice-*-saturday-exits.csv); paired-golden watch: every golden the flip moves, run PAIRED (flags off vs on) at the promotion PR's pinned build (table in PR body + dev/experiments/exit-basis-flip-2026-09-03/).")
 (window_id top3000-2000-2026-arc-and-record-26y) (baseline_label stale-friday-open-exit)
 (variants
  (((label record-08-24-stale-open) (config_hash exit-stale-skip-false)
    (aggregate
     (((total_return_pct 0.0) (max_drawdown_pct 0.0)))))
   ((label record-08-24-repriced-monday-open-first-order) (config_hash exit-nextopen-skip-false-firstorder)
    (aggregate
     (((total_return_pct 0.0) (max_drawdown_pct 0.0)))))))
 (verdict Inconclusive)
 (notes
  "READ THE VERDICT FIELD CAREFULLY. NOT an Accept: verdict type is the closed variant Accept | Reject | Inconclusive; Inconclusive is the house label for a human-gated R3 override (precedents 2026-08-24-stops-basis-book-faithful, 2026-08-18-entry-ticket-clock26-promotion). The variants table carries 0.0 placeholders: the evidence is first-order dollar repricing, not a backtest aggregate, and is recorded here in prose rather than invented as a return figure. WHAT HAPPENED: user approved both flips 2026-09-03 as ONE exit-basis correctness correction, explicitly framed as fidelity-not-performance (priorities doc P0: 'correctness fixes, not strategy mechanisms, but they move every golden'). EVIDENCE BASIS, all committed under dev/experiments/arc-rerun-2026-09-01/: (D1) 2192/2192 volume_eject, 154/154 laggard_rotation and 148/668 stop_loss exits in the 08-21 arc run were Saturday-dated at Friday's open; the record convention shows the same shape (269/269 laggard exits, 98/503 stops). First-order repricing at the next trading open, quantities fixed: arc 08-21 +$524,745; record 08-24 -$601,280 (stops -$336,865, laggards -$262,955); arc fresh 09-02 +$1,051,441. The defect moves the two arms in OPPOSITE directions (ejected weak-volume breakouts keep rising into Monday; the record's Friday stop/laggard triggers are selloffs that continue Monday), so it is not a neutral timing shift. (D2) 261 of 668 stop-losses exited within one day; 173 were the pure artifact (entry-day low pierced the stop, bar closed ABOVE it, sold next open above the stop; net +$45k in dollars but 5.7% of all breakout entries destroyed on day one). Both fixes verified absent at 5y and 26y with the flags armed (#2642, #2644 test plans + validators V13/V14 in #2641). FAITHFULNESS: D1 is a fill-assumption change only (spine untouched); D2 is bar-alignment hygiene, book section 5.1 places the protective stop to be honoured from inception FORWARD, a stop cannot be hit by price action that occurred before the shares were owned (weinstein-faithful-core W1/W2). CONSEQUENCE FOR EVERY EARLIER EXIT-LEVER VERDICT: project_lever_reads_invert_on_fixed_sim, eject-off read +48pp on the defective sim and +0.2pp with D1/D2 armed (2019-23); every pre-09-02 exit-lever verdict (eject on/off, stop width, TTL/clock, laggard timing) is suspect and must be re-measured on this basis. DEVIATIONS FROM THE NORMAL GATE, declared: (1) no WF-CV surface and no confirmation grid (promotion-confirmation.md), the flip corrects a measurement defect rather than promoting a mechanism, and a surface run on the defective basis cannot rank it; (2) no ledger Accept (R3), this entry is the record. BLAST RADIUS: every golden that exits a position moves (all strategy cells; Bah_benchmark cells do not); re-pinned PAIRED in the promotion PR per config-default-blast-radius, old arm = both flags pinned false at the same build. FOLLOW-UPS OWED: re-measure the exit levers named above on the fixed basis; re-run the record baseline (#2503 lineage) so the canonical 26y record is on the fixed basis; the warehouse splice gate (#2646) before any 2004/2006/2014/2021-window level claim."))
